# graphtope SG5 reference - the K and F unit interiors, room-labelled
# Provenance (plan risk R1 mitigation): RECONSTRUCTED, not measured.
#   * dimensions from the imported model / module: bay 3.66 m, unit depth
#     8.42 m, K section 8.0 m (5.0 living + 3.0 gallery), gallery strip 1.7 m
#     (U_units_realised.obj's mezzanine strips), stair 1.0 m;
#   * room arrangement from the published Dom Narkomfin section (Ginzburg,
#     type 2F units) as documented in the repo (spec 7.6.2, plan 5.3):
#     K rises off the corridor - double-height living, sleeping gallery over
#     the corridor end, internal stair at the bay end; F enters at corridor
#     level and drops a floor (the l_section) - kitchen/bath in the interlock
#     band beside the entry (the volume below that band belongs to the
#     interlocked neighbour, hence the L-shaped section).
# Conventions: o <K_unit|F_unit>_<room>; y+ is away from the corridor plane.
# The face-adjacency of these boxes is exactly the default G_U / G_L
# adjacency (audited - no touches without grammar edges).

